{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "87b6aa1a-117f-4c2a-901c-e63c924d8382",
    "name": "ClaimAssist Insurance-AI Platform - End to End",
    "description": "End-to-end debugging collection for the insurance-ai (ClaimAssist) microservices platform: discovery-service (Eureka), config-service (Spring Cloud Config), api-gateway, customer-service, claims-service and agent-service.\n\n## How to use this\n1. Bring the stack up (docker-compose.yml, or run each service's Application class locally with SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=local). Confirm everything is green in folder **00 - Infra Health Checks**.\n2. Run folder **01 - Auth** in order (Signup -> Authorize -> Callback). This populates the collection variables access_token / refresh_token / customer_id that every other request re-uses automatically (collection-level Bearer auth).\n3. Work through **02 -> 05** top to bottom - each folder's requests are ordered so that earlier responses (policy_id, claim_id) feed later requests via test scripts.\n4. **06 - API Gateway** is included last and documents a couple of known routing gaps in the current gateway config rather than a golden path - read its folder description before relying on it.\n\nImport the companion environment file alongside this collection and select it in the top-right environment picker before running anything.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "57155386",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/57155386-87b6aa1a-117f-4c2a-901c-e63c924d8382?source=collection_link"
  },
